tate_Get and _GetUnchecked: tstate->context written (tsContextWrite)"] [129 2 "// PyTraceMalloc_Track(domain, ptr, size) and PyTraceMalloc_Untrack(domain, ptr) (Python/tracemalloc.c): a C block's"] [130 2 "// trace in tracemalloc's tables, -2 when it is not tracing (594-1 (a): test_tracemalloc's TestCAPI)"] [137 2 "// PyUnstable_Object_ClearWeakRefsNoCallbacks (Objects/weakrefobject.c): the referent's weak references cleared, no"] [138 2 "// callback called, nothing for a type without weak references"] [145 2 "// the error indicator's setters need the thread state (errors.c's _PyThreadState_GET, then the exception's"] [146 2 "// creation)"] [148 16 "// a wrapper above (PyThreadState_Get's context), else the native"] [163 1 "// The debug hooks on the allocators (Objects/obmalloc.c's _PyMem_DebugRaw*, PYTHONMALLOC=debug, malloc_debug,"] [164 1 "// pymalloc_debug or mimalloc_debug): a block of the RAW ('r') and MEM ('m') domains is laid out as CPython's,"] [165 1 "// [size (8, big-endian), the API id, 7 FORBIDDENBYTEs, the data (CLEANBYTEs), 8 FORBIDDENBYTEs], checked when freed"] [166 1 "// or reallocated (a wrong API or a pad byte overwritten: the block dumped, then the fatal error), and MEM and OBJ"] [167 1 "// ('o') check the thread state (_PyMem_DebugCheckGIL). OBJ's blocks keep the world's layout: pyi's C objects are"] [168 1 "// made and freed through it."] [178 21 "// 0 unknown, 1 on, 2 off"] [183 1 "// debugHooks is whether PYTHONMALLOC asks for the debug hooks."] [195 1 "// debugCheckGIL is _PyMem_DebugCheckGIL."] [202 1 "// debugAlloc is _PyMem_DebugRawAlloc over the world's allocator (raw: the domain's default allocation of size bytes)."] [235 1 "// debugSize is the size a debug block's header records."] [244 1 "// debugDump is _PyObject_DebugDumpAddress, then _PyMem_DumpTraceback's line without tracemalloc's traces."] [314 1 "// debugCheckAddress is _PyMem_DebugCheckAddress: the API id, the leading and the trailing pad bytes."] [335 1 "// debugDomain is the domain d's operation i (malloc, calloc, realloc, free) through the debug hooks over the world's"] [336 1 "// allocator; ok false when the hooks are off or the block is none of theirs (the domain's default runs)."] [387 1 "// debugFree fills a checked block with DEADBYTEs and gives it back to the world's allocator."] [395 1 "// Py_TPFLAGS_HAVE_VECTORCALL across the classes over C types (Objects/typeobject.c, queue 594: test_call's TestPEP590):"] [396 1 "// a class inherits it from its C base when no class before that base in its MRO defines __call__ (inherit_slots), and"] [397 1 "// setting __call__ on a C type clears it there (update_one_slot's slot_tp_call: a generic __call__ is incompatible"] [398 1 "// with vectorcall), the type then called through its __call__, its subclasses' slots refilled."] [414 1 "// callSetOnCType is ExtTypeAttrSet: __call__ set on a C type."] [429 2 "// the classes over t that C has seen: their tp_flags again (a C type of their own keeps its own)"] [455 2 "// a C-born object keeps its Go finalizer on its life (newCObj), not on itself: py tracks it for its weak references"] [459 1 "// tstate->context (Include/cpython/pystate.h, LP64: offsetof(PyThreadState, context), gcc on CPython 3.14.10's headers):"] [460 1 "// the thread's current context, written when C fetches the thread state and held while it is there; a context C"] [461 1 "// cleared (Py_CLEAR(tstate->context): _testcapi's clear_context_stack, queue 594) is the thread's no more. A context's"] [462 1 "// ctx_prev (offset 16) is its proxy's zeroed word."] [467 1 "// tsContextWrite writes the thread's context into the thread state at ts."] [487 1 "// tsContextDone takes the thread state's context back when the outermost C entry returns (capiLeave): cleared by C,"] [488 1 "// the thread's is cleared."] [499 27 "// C's Py_CLEAR gave the reference back"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[48 39] [53 35] [140 23] [213 12] [213 26] [217 23] [217 39] [224 20] [224 32] [227